      "problem": "Find the value of $\\textrm{i}^{-2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, using the laws of exponents, we can write\n\n$$\n\\textrm{i}^{-2}=\\dfrac{1}{\\textrm{i}^2}.\n$$\n\nWe now recall that $\\textrm{i}^2 = -1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\textrm{i}^2} = \\dfrac{1}{(-1)} = -1.\n$$",
